opennyai_summary.facts:
The New Grain Market and the Link Road were to be constructed by the Market Committee, Rewari, which is the appellant herein.
The Land Acquisition Collector, by an Award dated 11.04.1986, awarded compensation at the rate of Rs. 16,000/- per acre.
The landowners, being dissatisfied, filed references under Section 18 of the Act, which were allowed in part vide an Award dated 30.08.1990 when the Reference Court fixed the compensation at the rate of Rs. 50,000/- per acre.
The claimant  landowners were also held entitled to solatium at the rate of 30%, an additional Market Committee, Rewari vs Nemi Chand (D) Thr.
The High Court held that -  a) The evidence brought on record shows that the acquired  land had the potentiality of residential and commercial  area;
 b) The acquired land was surrounded by schools, markets,
 educational institutions etc.;
 c) Reference Court was not justified in rejecting the  exemplars of Sale Deeds (Exhibit P-1 and Exhibit P-6)
 whereby some small pieces of land located near the acquired  land, were sold at the rate of Rs.9.60 lakhs per acre;
 d) The parcels of lands which were sold vide Sale Deeds  (Exhibit P-1 and Exhibit P-6) were of commercial value,
 hence 60% deduction on the amount assessed will be  appropriate;
 e) These two Sale Deeds were relevant piece of evidence as  both were executed prior to Notification under Section 4 of  the Act.
